    "message": "fix(php): capture grouped use imports\n\n`use Vendor\\Package\\{A, B};` (and the `use function` / `use const`\nvariants) never produced IMPORTS relationships: the PHP query only\nmatched `namespace_use_clause (qualified_name)`, but a group's shared\nprefix is a separate `namespace_name` and each member is a bare\n`namespace_use_clause (name)` — so every member import was silently\ndropped and calls like `new A()` went unresolved.\n\nAdd a grouped-use pattern that captures the prefix (`@import.prefix`)\nand each member clause (`@import.clause`), and rebuild each FQCN from\nprefix + the clause's FIRST name child (a second name child is an `as`\nalias and must never become an import). The emitted modName/importRaw\nmatch the single-clause form, so grouped imports resolve exactly like\ntheir comma-separated equivalents.\n\nRegression tests: per-member capture, alias exclusion, and end-to-end\nresolution of a grouped import. Fail-before verified on main.",
